[38;5;231m⏺[39m Bob's Claude asked how [38;5;153mcreateTask[39m in [38;5;153msrc/store.js[39m picks ids, and I sent it the answer without changing anything. The
  message is queued in its session.

  - [1mHow ids work:[0m a counter at the top of the file starts at 1 and goes up by one for each new task ([38;5;153msrc/store.js:5[39m,
    [38;5;153msrc/store.js:8[39m). It goes back to 1 only when [38;5;153mreset()[39m runs, and since the store is in memory, it also starts over
    when the process restarts.
  - [1mWhat matters for paging:[0m ids never repeat, but timestamps do, because [38;5;153mseed()[39m gives every 3 tasks the same timestamp.
    Paging on the timestamp alone would skip or repeat rows. Paging on the id, or on the timestamp with the id as a
    tiebreaker, avoids that. That's relevant to the paging question Bob raised in #4.

